  "summary": "Toledo City Council delayed a vote on a resolution calling for the city to terminate its Flock contracts, deactivate cameras, and delete data, after a motion to bypass two readings failed 7-5. The delay comes as an independent audit of the city's Flock use is underway; the resolution returns to the agenda Nov. 4.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Toledo City Council will wait at least two more weeks to consider a resolution calling for the city to terminate its contracts with Flock Group Inc., the company behind its controversial license plate-reading cameras.",
      "paragraph_idx": 0
    },
    {
      "quote": "The resolution, which calls on Mayor Wade Kapszukiewicz's administration to terminate the agreements, deactivate or remove Flock equipment, and delete data collected by the company, will return to council's agenda Nov. 4.",
      "paragraph_idx": 2
    },
    {
      "quote": "It's Flock's problem to provide the guardrails to make sure that there's safety for our residents, that there is protection of our residents' data",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    }
  ],
